      "description": "Watch Fenerbahce vs Konyaspor highlights and goals from Süper Lig on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 22, 2026. High Stakes in the Süper Lig On August 22, 2026, Fenerbahce faced off against Konyaspor in a match that promised tactical intrigue and attacking flair. Both sets of players took to the pitch under the lights, eager to stake their claim in this pivotal Süper Lig encounter. A Chaotic First Half The match ignited early as Ebrima Colley struck for Konyaspor in the 11th minute, assisted by Yhoan Andzouana . However, the lead was short-lived as Vedat Muriqi leveled the score just minutes later. Fenerbahce quickly seized control of the momentum; Mason Greenwood put his team in the lead at the 20-minute mark, even overcoming the disappointment of a missed penalty in that same sequence. The hosts continued to pile on the pressure, with Marco Asensio finding the net in the 33rd minute, courtesy of a clever assist from Greenwood . Maintaining the Momentum Coming out of the break, Fenerbahce looked to put the game beyond reach. Mason Greenwood added his second of the match in the 49th minute, latching onto a Vedat Muriqi delivery to extend the lead. As the game progressed, the intensity grew, leading to a yellow card for Enis Bardhi in the 61st minute. Despite a late consolation goal from Deniz Turuc deep into stoppage time, the home side held firm to secure an impressive victory, concluding a thrilling afternoon of football."
